From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] init: do not set ro.kernel.version

SetKernelVersion() sets ro.kernel.version from init's own uname() before
any rc file is read. With patches/kernel/core/0008 the kernel reports a
configured release to apps, while init sees the real one. The property
has no entry in property_contexts, so it is labelled default_prop, which
apps can read, and it would contradict the release they are told.

The only users in rootdir/init.rc are the late-fs blocks for 4.19 and
5.4 kernels, which do not apply to this device. Keep the function and
drop the call.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [goes with patches/kernel/core/0008]
---
 init/init.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init/init.cpp b/init/init.cpp
index aec2688..1477925 100644
--- a/init/init.cpp
+++ b/init/init.cpp
@@ -738,7 +738,7 @@ static void SetUsbController(bool run_loop) {
 
 /// Set ro.kernel.version property to contain the major.minor pair as returned
 /// by uname(2).
-static void SetKernelVersion() {
+[[maybe_unused]] static void SetKernelVersion() {
     struct utsname uts;
     unsigned int major, minor;
 
@@ -1190,7 +1190,8 @@ int SecondStageMain(int argc, char** argv) {
     } else {
         usb_controller_thread = std::make_unique<std::thread>(&SetUsbController, true);
     }
-    SetKernelVersion();
+    // ro.kernel.version is not set: apps can read it, and it would contradict the release
+    // the kernel reports to them.
 
     const BuiltinFunctionMap& function_map = GetBuiltinFunctionMap();
     Action::set_function_map(&function_map);
